.SH NAME
sudoconsole-policy - Inspect and validate the active policy


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsudoconsole policy [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
policy lets you preview and verify the rules sudoconsole applies
before any sudo command runs. Use it to understand which binaries are
blocked, to dry-run a single command against the active configuration,
and to lint custom patterns before they take effect.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for policy


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--cache-timeout\fP=0
	sudo cache timeout in seconds (60-3600); overrides config file

.PP
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the TOML config file (default: platform XDG/Application Support location)

.PP
\fB--format\fP=""
	output format: human or json (overrides config file)

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP=""
	log level: silent, error, warn, info, debug (overrides config file)


